<div class="deck">

    <section class="slide slide-cover" id="slide-1">
        <span class="slide-num">01</span>
        <div class="slide-inner">
            <span class="eyebrow">A proposal by Ian Allan, Founder, Saved.</span>
            <h1>Diploma in Resilient Technologies</h1>
            <p class="lead">Technology education and the fight for the East Coast, and any constrained region where the standard tech stack doesn&rsquo;t serve.</p>
            <div class="stat-strip">
                <span><strong>L5</strong>NZQCF Level</span>
                <span><strong>120</strong>Credits</span>
                <span><strong>8</strong>Credentials</span>
                <span><strong>1&nbsp;yr</strong>Duration</span>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="slide" id="slide-2">
        <span class="slide-num">02</span>
        <div class="slide-inner">
            <span class="eyebrow">The problem</span>
            <h2>Converging technology pressures</h2>
            <div class="slide-cols slide-cols-3">
                <div>
                    <h3>Digital rents keep rising</h3>
                    <p>Market-leading online services are heavily subsidised by investor capital. And when that bargain ends the services get worse, the rent goes up, and inequalities are exacerbated.</p>
                </div>
                <div>
                    <h3>Regions are precarious</h3>
                    <p>We can't take connectivity, power, or corporate goodwill for granted. Climate events, isolation, and economic imbalances mean resilience has to be built locally.</p>
                </div>
                <div>
                    <h3>AI has upended things</h3>
                    <p>Students must be AI-fluent to be employable, while the same tools are pushing down on the entry-level roles they&rsquo;re training for.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="slide" id="slide-3">
        <span class="slide-num">03</span>
        <div class="slide-inner">
            <span class="eyebrow">The opportunity</span>
            <h2>There is no qualification like this yet</h2>
            <p class="lead">Imagine the technologist who can reclaim machines, stand up their own servers, host their own AI models, integrate physical sensors, fly drones, and configure solar; all in service of their community.</p>
            <p class="lead"><strong>That person has no tertiary pathway in Aotearoa yet.</strong></p>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="slide" id="slide-4">
        <span class="slide-num">04</span>
        <div class="slide-inner">
            <span class="eyebrow">The solution</span>
            <h2>Introducing the diploma</h2>
            <p class="lead">A studio-based programme where graduates can build, own, and operate resilient technologies for themselves and their communities.</p>
            <div class="stats-grid">
                <div class="stat"><span class="stat-value">L5</span><span class="stat-label">NZQCF Level</span></div>
                <div class="stat"><span class="stat-value">120</span><span class="stat-label">Credits</span></div>
                <div class="stat"><span class="stat-value">8</span><span class="stat-label">Credentials</span></div>
                <div class="stat"><span class="stat-value">1&nbsp;yr</span><span class="stat-label">Duration</span></div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="slide" id="slide-5">
        <span class="slide-num">05</span>
        <div class="slide-inner">
            <span class="eyebrow">How it works</span>
            <h2>The studio model</h2>
            <p class="lead">A shared space and a tight group challenging one another with the same rhythm as a design or maker studio.</p>
            <div class="delivery-grid">
                <div class="delivery-item"><span class="delivery-label">Delivery</span><span class="delivery-value">Studio-based, project-centred</span></div>
                <div class="delivery-item"><span class="delivery-label">Structure</span><span class="delivery-value">2 semesters &middot; 8 credentials &times; 15 credits</span></div>
                <div class="delivery-item"><span class="delivery-label">Assessment</span><span class="delivery-value">Live demonstration, Q&amp;A, real-time modification, real deployment</span></div>
                <div class="delivery-item"><span class="delivery-label">Articulation</span><span class="delivery-value">Pathway to Level 6/7</span></div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="slide" id="slide-6">
        <span class="slide-num">06</span>
        <div class="slide-inner">
            <span class="eyebrow">Semester one &mdash; Sovereign Self</span>
            <h2>Own your computing</h2>
            <div class="credential-list">
                <div><span class="credential-code">C1</span><div><strong>Foundations</strong><p>Reclaim a machine, migrate off dependency.</p></div></div>
                <div><span class="credential-code">C2</span><div><strong>Open Operating Systems</strong><p>Linux, from daily-driver to self-hosted server.</p></div></div>
                <div><span class="credential-code">C3</span><div><strong>Applied Open Source AI</strong><p>Run your own models, own your data.</p></div></div>
                <div><span class="credential-code">C4</span><div><strong>Open Web Fundamentals</strong><p>Build and deploy real sites, no lock-in.</p></div></div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="slide" id="slide-7">
        <span class="slide-num">07</span>
        <div class="slide-inner">
            <span class="eyebrow">Semester two &mdash; Sovereign Service</span>
            <h2>Serve your region</h2>
            <div class="credential-list">
                <div><span class="credential-code">C5</span><div><strong>Physical Computing &amp; Sensing</strong><p>Low-cost sensing, deployed and connected.</p></div></div>
                <div><span class="credential-code">C6</span><div><strong>Fabrication &amp; Electronics</strong><p>Circuits, soldering, 3D printing, real builds.</p></div></div>
                <div><span class="credential-code">C7</span><div><strong>Community Energy Systems</strong><p>Off-grid solar to community micro-grids.</p></div></div>
                <div><span class="credential-code">C8</span><div><strong>Aerial Operations</strong><p>Lawful drone flying, mapping briefs.</p></div></div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="slide" id="slide-8">
        <span class="slide-num">08</span>
        <div class="slide-inner">
            <span class="eyebrow">Assessment</span>
            <h2>Proof in doing</h2>
            <p class="lead">AI has broken conventional written assessment, and not everyone's academically-minded anyway. So in this diploma every credential is assessed the same way:</p>
            <p class="lead"><strong>Live demonstrations, professional conversations, real-time modifications, real deployments.</strong></p>
            <p class="lead">You can&rsquo;t fake showing up and explaining your own work.</p>
        </div>
    </section>

